{"author":"Claude","author_email":"noreply@anthropic.com","data":{"alias":"bilingual-capitalist-caecilian","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\n`rebar init` (auto-init / `rebar init --silent`) created a **fresh, empty** local\ntracker on a new `tickets` branch even though an authoritative `tickets` branch with\nreal ticket history already existed on the configured sync remote (`origin`). The local\ntracker (`.tickets-tracker`) diverged from `origin/tickets`, so every read command\n(`rebar list`, `rebar show`, `search`, …) returns an EMPTY store, hiding all existing\ntickets. Any writes made now land on the divergent local branch and cannot be\nfast-forward-pushed back to `origin/tickets`.\n\nRoot contributing factor: fetching the remote `tickets` branch times out\n(>100s) through the agent git proxy, so init silently fell back to bootstrapping a fresh\nstore instead of failing loudly or retrying.\n\n## Impact\n\n- `rebar list --status=open --type=bug` (and all other reads) return `[]` — existing\n  work is invisible.\n- New ticket events are written to a divergent local `tickets` history that will not\n  fast-forward onto `origin/tickets`, risking lost or conflicting events.\n- Silent data-hiding: no error is surfaced to the operator; the store simply looks empty.\n\n## Environment\n\n- Remote execution environment (Claude Code on the web), ephemeral container.\n- Primary working directory: `/home/user/rebar`\n- Platform: Linux 6.18.5\n- Checked-out code branch: `claude/open-bugs-list-m4iu76`\n- rebar version: `nava-rebar 0.10.1`\n- `origin` remote: `http://local_proxy@127.0.0.1:41729/git/navapbc/rebar`\n- Outbound git/HTTPS goes through the pre-configured agent proxy.\n- No `.venv` was present at session start; `rebar` was not on `PATH`. Bootstrapped with\n  `python3 -m venv .venv && make install`.\n- Config (relevant): `sync.remote = origin`, `sync.pull = on`, `sync.push = always`.\n\n## Reproduction — exact commands and observed output\n\n1. rebar not installed / not on PATH:\n\n   ```\n   $ rebar list --status=open --type=bug\n   /bin/bash: line 1: rebar: command not found\n   $ python3 -m rebar list ...\n   /usr/local/bin/python3: No module named rebar\n   $ ls .venv\n   ls: cannot access '.venv': No such file or directory\n   ```\n\n2. Bootstrap env:\n\n   ```\n   $ python3 -m venv .venv && make install\n   Successfully installed ... nava-rebar-0.10.1 ...\n   ```\n\n3. Store reports not initialized, then init produced an EMPTY store:\n\n   ```\n   $ rebar list --status=open --type=bug\n   Error: ticket system not initialized. Run 'rebar init' first (auto-init requires an interactive terminal).\n   $ rebar init --silent\n   (no output)\n   $ rebar list --status=open --type=bug\n   []\n   $ rebar list                       # all statuses\n   []\n   ```\n\n4. But a real `tickets` branch exists on `origin`, and it is actively moving (other\n   agents writing to it) — two `ls-remote` reads minutes apart returned different tips:\n\n   ```\n   $ git ls-remote origin 'refs/heads/tickets'\n   aa498170daa39767eab3282f505700e30bbed1ea  refs/heads/tickets   # first check\n   ...\n   $ git ls-remote origin 'refs/heads/tickets'\n   4b51478a14c150a1032a8b2988d1524bfda1da54  refs/heads/tickets   # minutes later\n   ```\n\n5. The local tracker worktree is a FRESH divergent branch (bootstrap commits only, none\n   of the remote history):\n\n   ```\n   $ git worktree list\n   /home/user/rebar               ... claude/open-bugs-list-m4iu76\n   /home/user/rebar/.tickets-tracker ... tickets\n\n   $ git -C .tickets-tracker log --oneline -n 6\n   37e8b02 chore: add .store-compat.json store-compatibility record (story 21dd)\n   ed99e08 chore: add .gitignore for env-id, state-cache, scratch, and reducer cache\n   936ec76 chore: add .gitattributes merge=ours for shared mutable root files (epic 97e7)\n   a7ad28d chore: add no-op .pre-commit-config.yaml (bug 27d8-b230)\n   94e48da chore: initialize ticket tracker\n   $ git -C .tickets-tracker rev-parse tickets\n   37e8b026cf61e04b651f29b849294f6d549c8210\n   ```\n\n   Local tip `37e8b02` shares no history with remote tip `4b51478a` → divergent.\n\n6. Fetching the remote `tickets` branch to reconverge TIMES OUT (reproduced multiple\n   times, both from the main checkout and from inside `.tickets-tracker`):\n\n   ```\n   $ git -C .tickets-tracker fetch origin tickets      # 100s timeout\n   Terminated   (exit 143)\n   $ git fetch origin tickets                          # 120s tool timeout\n   Command timed out after 2m 0s\n   ```\n\n   `rebar fsck` reports the (empty) local store as healthy, so nothing flags the problem:\n\n   ```\n   $ rebar fsck\n   ensures: 6/6 applied\n   authorship: 0 signed, 0 unsigned event(s)\n   fsck complete: no issues found\n   ```\n\n## Confirmed divergence and fetch-latency (observed this session)\n\nA full (unbounded-timeout) background fetch of `origin/tickets` eventually SUCCEEDED,\nwhich let me quantify both the divergence and the latency that caused the fallback:\n\n- The remote `tickets` branch is large and event-sourced — **49,301 commits**:\n\n  ```\n  $ git -C .tickets-tracker rev-list --count origin/tickets\n  49301\n  ```\n\n- The local auto-initialized tracker and `origin/tickets` share **NO common ancestor**\n  (definitively a fresh, divergent store — not a fast-forwardable lag):\n\n  ```\n  $ git -C .tickets-tracker merge-base tickets origin/tickets\n  (no output; exit 1) -> NO COMMON ANCESTOR (divergent)\n  $ git rev-parse origin/tickets      # authoritative\n  80ec6ba00f4ce4daef8dada62c8056e003e8ef92\n  $ git -C .tickets-tracker rev-parse tickets   # local fresh-init\n  dcb0b1ac7ff39999016a7aa73eeef9644b1e0247\n  ```\n\n- The branch is **actively written by other agents** — its tip moved four times across\n  this single session: `aa498170…` → `4b51478a…` → `80ec6ba…`, etc.\n\n- **Fetch latency is the trigger:** `git fetch origin tickets` was killed at 100s and at\n  the 120s tool limit, but the same fetch run WITHOUT a kill-timeout (in the background)\n  completed successfully in several minutes. So the branch is reachable; init simply gave\n  up (or its bounded fetch timed out) and fell back to a fresh empty store rather than\n  waiting/retrying. A bounded init fetch against a 49k-commit branch over the proxy is not\n  enough headroom.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n`rebar init` MUST NOT silently bootstrap a fresh empty store when the configured sync\nremote already has a `tickets` branch. It should either:\n\n- fetch/adopt `origin/tickets` as the local tracker's base (the store is non-empty), or\n- fail loudly (non-zero exit, clear message) when it cannot reach/fetch the existing\n  remote `tickets` branch, instead of falling back to a divergent empty store.\n\nAdditionally, the remote-`tickets` fetch through the agent proxy should be made\nresilient (retry/backoff, longer timeout) rather than silently abandoned.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `rebar init` / auto-init detects an existing `tickets` branch on `sync.remote`\n      before creating a new one, and bases the local tracker on it (reads return the\n      existing tickets, not `[]`).\n- [ ] When the existing remote `tickets` branch cannot be fetched, init fails loudly\n      (clear error + non-zero exit) instead of silently bootstrapping a divergent empty\n      store.\n- [ ] A health check (`fsck`/`validate`) detects and reports a local `tickets` tracker\n      that has diverged from `origin/tickets` (no shared history / cannot fast-forward),\n      rather than reporting \"no issues found\".\n- [ ] Regression coverage: a test simulates a reachable, non-empty remote `tickets`\n      branch and asserts init does not produce an empty divergent store.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Filed per operator request while investigating \"show me a list of open bugs\" returning\n  an empty list.\n- Because the local store is currently divergent and the remote fetch times out, this\n  ticket may itself be written to the divergent local `tickets` history and may not sync\n  to `origin/tickets` until the underlying fetch/reconverge issue is resolved.","id":"01e8-302b-ab8f-4220","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["store","init","sync","data-integrity"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"rebar init bootstrapped a fresh empty tracker while origin/tickets already existed (divergent store, reads return [])"},"env_id":"cba2dbd1-cb95-4a2d-bffc-115bee6bc264","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785290833779065231,"uuid":"3a3804b6-6eb2-4279-946c-de9b9477bfca"}